{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_37393ad0ce834d79ad0e6397","type":"tool_result","content":"title:\tfix(e2e): scaffold.runtime blocked on main — the readiness fixture hardcodes garnet_resp while the scaffold default cache is redis\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\trickylabs\nlabels:\tarea:aspire, area:cli, area:tooling, gate:e2e, orchestrator:fixes, priority:p0, status:impl-eval, type:fix\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t0.0.7\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t1870\n--\n> **Superseded diagnosis.** The first version of this issue attributed the failure to the fixture\n> hardcoding `garnet_resp` while the scaffold default cache is `redis`. That is wrong: plugin install\n> provisions a `garnet` cache, so `garnet_resp` **is** emitted. The real cause is below. The earlier\n> reasoning is left out rather than preserved, because acting on it would have produced a redesign\n> that fixed nothing.\n\n## Symptom\n\n`scaffold.runtime` and `scaffold.runtime.sqlite` are both blocked on `main` at gate\n`runtime.readiness-fixture`, immediately after `runtime.flow-b-fixture` passes:\n\n```\n> runtime.readiness-fixture: Wire dead-port readiness fixture\n  FAILED 79ms\nerror: Uncaught (in promise) Error: generated register-infrastructure helper has no garnet health-check marker\n    at injectListenerFaultHealthChecks (packages/cli/e2e/src/application/gates/scaffold/runtime/prepare-readiness-fixture.ts:63:11)\n```\n\nBoth hosted tiers of run\n[`33484656019`](https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/actions/runs/33484656019). Not attributable to\nthe PR it ran on — `git diff origin/main <head> -- prepare-readiness-fixture.ts` is empty.\n\n## Root cause — a #1837 regression, proven by generation\n\nThe E2E project has **two** caches, not one:\n\n- `redis` — from `netscript init` (`SCAFFOLD_DEFAULTS.CACHE_BACKEND`), `Engine: Redis`,\n  `Mode: Container`.\n- `garnet` — appended during plugin install by\n  `PluginWorkspaceMutator.ensureSharedCache(projectRoot, cacheKey = 'garnet')`\n  (`workspace-mutator.ts:610-637`, called from `install-plugin.ts:231` and\n  `install-local-plugin.ts:174`) for every plugin that needs KV, as\n  `{ Enabled: true, Engine: 'Garnet', Mode: 'Auto' }`.\n\nGenerating at exact `d2b33a09b` with that real two-cache config emits:\n\n```\n  builder.addHealthCheck(\"redis_resp\", async () => {\n  await cache_0.withHealthCheck(\"redis_resp\");\n  caches.set(\"redis\", cache_0);\n    builder.addHealthCheck(\"garnet_resp\", async () => {\n    await cache_1.withHealthCheck(\"garnet_resp\");\n    caches.set(\"garnet\", cache_1);\n    builder.addHealthCheck(\"garnet_resp\", async () => {\n    await cache_1.withHealthCheck(\"garnet_resp\");\n    caches.set(\"garnet\", cache_1);\n```\n\n**`garnet_resp` is emitted twice** — once in each arm of the `Mode: 'Auto'` branch\n`generate-register-infrastructure.ts` emits (`if (shouldUseContainerCache()) { container } else {\ngarnet executable }`). Only one arm runs; both are emitted. That is correct generator behaviour.\n\n`uniqueHealthAttachment(source, key)` returns `undefined` unless `attachments.length === 1`, so two\noccurrences yield `undefined` and `injectListenerFaultHealthChecks` throws.\n\n**#1837 introduced this.** Before it the check was `source.includes(<whole marker line>)` — a\nduplicate-tolerant substring test that the Auto dual-arm emission satisfied. #1837 replaced it with a\nstrict uniqueness requirement that `Mode: 'Auto'` inherently violates. This is the same class as\n#1863: a #1837 hardening that a generator-output shape silently invalidates.\n\nThe thrown message is also wrong — the condition is \"not exactly one\", not \"none\" — which is what\nmade the first diagnosis of this issue plausible and wrong.\n\n### Why it passed on 2026-08-31 and fails now\n\n`runtime.readiness-fixture` and `runtime.wait.garnet` both passed in run\n[`33425281612`](https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/actions/runs/33425281612) at head\n`bd239f916`, whose base predates #1837. The duplicate-tolerant substring test accepted the dual-arm\nemission. #1837 landed at `1f50c98ce`, and the very next hosted runtime run fails. The anomaly is\nresolved; no further investigation is needed.\n\n## Fix\n\nHandle **N ≥ 1** attachments per health key in `prepare-readiness-fixture.ts`:\n\n- Find **all** attachments for the real key.\n- **Zero remains an error**, fail-closed, with a message that actually says \"no attachment\".\n- **More than one is legitimate.** Inject the test-only check beside **every** occurrence, using that\n  occurrence's own resource binding, because whichever arm executes at runtime must carry the\n  test-only check. Selecting a single arm would leave the fixture inert on the other.\n- Distinguish \"absent\" from \"not unique\" in the error messages.\n- Apply the same shape to the postgres key rather than special-casing it.\n- The `already registered` guard must still trip if a test-only key appears anywhere.\n\n`GARNET_REAL_HEALTH_KEY = 'garnet_resp'` is **correct** and stays: `ensureSharedCache` provisions\nexactly that cache key. Do not rewrite the fixture to discover the cache backend, and do not touch\n`listener-readiness-gates.ts`, `listener-unreachable-fixture.ts`, or `ASPIRE_RESOURCE.GARNET`.\n\n### Ceiling\n\n```\npackages/cli/e2e/src/application/gates/scaffold/runtime/prepare-readiness-fixture.ts\npackages/cli/e2e/tests/application/gates/prepare-readiness-fixture_test.ts\n```\n\nNo `packages/cli/src/**` change: the generator is behaving correctly.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] `injectListenerFaultHealthChecks` accepts N ≥ 1 attachments for a health key and injects the test-only check beside every occurrence, with the correct per-occurrence resource binding.\n- [ ] Zero attachments still fails closed, and \"absent\" and \"not unique\" produce distinguishable messages.\n- [ ] A RED commit reproduces the failure from **real generator output for the two-cache config** (`redis` Container + `garnet` `Mode: 'Auto'`); a RED built on a single-cache project does not reproduce what CI hits.\n- [ ] A test proves the single-attachment (`Mode: 'Container'`) case still works.\n- [ ] `runtime.readiness-fixture` executes and passes in both hosted tiers.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3eaf1e2a-824c-4c73-a5b7-15263968c283","uuid":"d561ca6e-c3d4-4098-8401-757f3c793f2d","timestamp":"2026-09-01T13:15:07.247Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"title:\tfix(e2e): scaffold.runtime blocked on main — the readiness fixture hardcodes garnet_resp while the scaffold default cache is redis\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\trickylabs\nlabels:\tarea:aspire, area:cli, area:tooling, gate:e2e, orchestrator:fixes, priority:p0, status:impl-eval, type:fix\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t0.0.7\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t1870\n--\n> **Superseded diagnosis.** The first version of this issue attributed the failure to the fixture\n> hardcoding `garnet_resp` while the scaffold default cache is `redis`. That is wrong: plugin install\n> provisions a `garnet` cache, so `garnet_resp` **is** emitted. The real cause is below. The earlier\n> reasoning is left out rather than preserved, because acting on it would have produced a redesign\n> that fixed nothing.\n\n## Symptom\n\n`scaffold.runtime` and `scaffold.runtime.sqlite` are both blocked on `main` at gate\n`runtime.readiness-fixture`, immediately after `runtime.flow-b-fixture` passes:\n\n```\n> runtime.readiness-fixture: Wire dead-port readiness fixture\n  FAILED 79ms\nerror: Uncaught (in promise) Error: generated register-infrastructure helper has no garnet health-check marker\n    at injectListenerFaultHealthChecks (packages/cli/e2e/src/application/gates/scaffold/runtime/prepare-readiness-fixture.ts:63:11)\n```\n\nBoth hosted tiers of run\n[`33484656019`](https://githu