{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_4329068c84ea43ad819510f7","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"base\":\"1e53e731a69336d206241a9cd42314b15ca65422\",\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n`scaffold.runtime` and `scaffold.runtime.sqlite` are blocked on `main` at gate\\n`runtime.readiness-fixture`. This restores the gate.\\n\\n**This is a second #1837 regression of the same class as #1863** — a hardening that a generator\\noutput shape silently invalidates. It is **not** a hardcoded-`garnet_resp` problem; that literal is\\ncorrect.\\n\\nCloses #1870\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\nThe E2E project carries **two** caches: `redis` from `netscript init`, and `garnet` appended during\\nplugin install by `PluginWorkspaceMutator.ensureSharedCache(root, 'garnet')`\\n(`workspace-mutator.ts:610-637`) as `{ Enabled: true, Engine: 'Garnet', Mode: 'Auto' }`.\\n\\nBecause that cache is `Mode: 'Auto'`, `generate-register-infrastructure.ts` emits the RESP health\\nattachment **twice** — once per arm of `if (shouldUseContainerCache()) { … } else { … }`. Generating\\nat exact `d2b33a09b` with that real config:\\n\\n```\\n  builder.addHealthCheck(\\\"redis_resp\\\", async () =\\u003e {\\n  await cache_0.withHealthCheck(\\\"redis_resp\\\");\\n    builder.addHealthCheck(\\\"garnet_resp\\\", async () =\\u003e {     \\u003c- container arm\\n    await cache_1.withHealthCheck(\\\"garnet_resp\\\");\\n    builder.addHealthCheck(\\\"garnet_resp\\\", async () =\\u003e {     \\u003c- executable arm\\n    await cache_1.withHealthCheck(\\\"garnet_resp\\\");\\n```\\n\\n#1837 replaced a duplicate-tolerant `source.includes(\\u003cwhole marker line\\u003e)` test with\\n`uniqueHealthAttachment`, which returns `undefined` unless there is exactly **one** attachment. Two\\narms ⇒ `undefined` ⇒ throw. The thrown message (\\\"no … marker\\\") misreports the actual condition\\n(\\\"not exactly one\\\"), which is why two earlier readings of this defect were wrong.\\n\\nThis matches the timeline exactly: the gate passed at `bd239f916` (base predates #1837) and fails on\\nthe first hosted runtime run after `1f50c98ce`.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n`healthAttachments()` now returns **every** attachment for a health key, and\\n`injectAtHealthAttachments()` splices the test-only block after each one — iterating in **descending\\noffset order** so earlier offsets stay valid, and using **that occurrence's own** resource binding.\\n\\nFail-closed behaviour is preserved and sharpened:\\n\\n- **Zero** attachments is still an error; the message now says \\\"attachment\\\" rather than \\\"marker\\\", so\\n  absent and not-unique are no longer conflated.\\n- The injected keys remain `TEST_ONLY_GARNET_HEALTH_KEY` / `TEST_ONLY_POSTGRES_HEALTH_KEY`.\\n- The \\\"already registered\\\" guard still trips if a test-only key appears anywhere.\\n- Postgres takes the same code path rather than a special case.\\n\\n`GARNET_REAL_HEALTH_KEY = 'garnet_resp'` is **unchanged** — it is correct. No cache-backend\\ndiscovery was added, no listener file was touched, and `ASPIRE_RESOURCE.GARNET` is untouched.\\n\\n## Why offsets, not `String.replace`\\n\\nAn earlier iteration of this fix used `injected.replace(attachment.statement, …)` per attachment.\\nBoth `Auto` arms emit a **byte-identical** statement, and `String.replace` with a string needle\\nreplaces only the first match — so it injected **twice into the container arm and not at all into\\nthe executable arm**. That would have passed CI (Docker present ⇒ container arm runs) while leaving\\nD-101 inert on the Docker-less path. Caught before commit by executing the injector against real\\ngenerator output.\\n\\nThe regression test therefore asserts **placement** — each real `garnet_resp` attachment is\\nimmediately followed by its own test-only registration, and the `} else {` boundary sits between\\nthem — not a total count. A count-only assertion passes under the bug.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\nRED and GREEN are separate commits, and the gate results below were measured **by the supervisor in\\nan isolated detached worktree at the exact head**, independently of the implementation session.\\n\\n| Head | Result |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| RED `e7e4e4dc5` — test-only, 1 file, +26 lines | exit **1**, 4 passed / 1 failed, failing with the exact production error `generated register-infrastructure helper has no garnet health-check marker` |\\n| GREEN `ce7dd440c` | exit **0**, 5 passed / 0 failed |\\n\\nThe RED reproduces the **CI** condition, not a synthetic one: it builds the fixture input from\\n`generateRegisterInfrastructure` with the real two-cache config.\\n\\n| Gate | Result | Detail |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| E2E gates suite (`run-deno-test.ts`) | **PASS** exit 0 | 108 passed / 0 failed |\\n| E2E workspace check (`run-deno-check.ts`) | **PASS** exit 0 | 187 files, 2 batches, 0 diagnostics |\\n| E2E workspace format (`run-deno-fmt.ts`) | **PASS** exit 0 | 187 processed, 0 findings, 0 refusals |\\n| Focused lint (`.../scaffold/runtime`) | **PASS** exit 0 | 13 files, 0 findings, 0 refusals |\\n| E2E workspace lint | **REFUSAL** exit 2 | `Package 'zod' not found in catalog` from the detached `desktop-native` fixture. **Pre-existing** — the identical refusal reproduces on clean `main` `d2b33a09b`. Recorded as REFUSAL, not PASS. |\\n| Lock hygiene | **PASS** | `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- deno.lock` empty |\\n\\nPlacement verified by execution against real generator output: one test-only registration in the\\ncontainer arm (lines 86-87) and one in the executable arm (104-105).\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nTwo product/test files plus run artifacts:\\n\\n```\\npackages/cli/e2e/src/application/gates/scaffold/runtime/prepare-readiness-fixture.ts\\npackages/cli/e2e/tests/application/gates/prepare-readiness-fixture_test.ts\\n.llm/runs/fix-readiness-fixture-cache-discovery--1870/**\\n```\\n\\nNo `packages/cli/src/**` change — the generator is behaving correctly. `deno.lock` untouched.\\n\\n## What this unblocks\\n\\n`runtime.readiness-fixture` is gate 36 of `scaffold.runtime`. While it fails, no PR can earn a\\nruntime receipt. Once this lands, PR #1865's `gate:e2e` can be rerun at its existing head to satisfy\\nits final acceptance box, and #1858's Garnet work becomes runtime-provable.\\n\\n## Definition of Done\\n\\n- [ ] `injectListenerFaultHealthChecks` accepts N ≥ 1 attachments for a health key and injects the test-only check beside every occurrence, with the correct per-occurrence resource binding.\\n- [ ] Zero attachments still fails closed, and \\\"absent\\\" and \\\"not unique\\\" produce distinguishable messages.\\n- [ ] A RED commit reproduces the failure from real generator output for the two-cache config (`redis` Container + `garnet` `Mode: 'Auto'`).\\n- [ ] A test proves the single-attachment (`Mode: 'Container'`) case still works.\\n- [ ] `runtime.readiness-fixture` executes and passes in both hosted tiers.\\n- [ ] `deno.lock` unchanged; no `packages/cli/src/**` change.\\n\",\"head\":\"7b5a31a807be4f9b2bb9a15acb7f22aa16d93c9d\",\"labels\":[\"type:fix\",\"area:cli\",\"status:impl-eval\",\"area:tooling\",\"area:aspire\",\"ci:full\",\"gate:e2e\",\"priority:p0\",\"orchestrator:fixes\"],\"milestone\":\"0.0.7\",\"state\":\"open\",\"title\":\"fix(cli): discover readiness fixture cache\"}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3eaf1e2a-824c-4c73-a5b7-15263968c283","uuid":"902cc5da-40c7-4752-8cdd-426fb4905f01","timestamp":"2026-09-01T13:15:15.108Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"base\":\"1e53e731a69336d206241a9cd42314b15ca65422\",\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n`scaffold.runtime` and `scaffold.runtime.sqlite` are blocked on `main` at gate\\n`runtime.readiness-fixture`. This restores the gate.\\n\\n**This is a second #1837 regression of the same class as #1863** — a hardening that a generator\\noutput shape silently invalidates. It is **not** a hardcoded-`garnet_resp` problem; that literal is\\ncorrect.\\n\\nCloses #1870\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\nThe E2E project carries